title: T1569-Impacket-SMBexec-Comspec-Remote-Service-Injection
id: 0f06a3a5-6a09-413f-8743-e6cf35561298
description: Utilising Application logs, based on research it appears EventCode 325 containing the ntds.dit filters out a lot of potential false positive noise revolving around this attack technique.
author: KJ
status: development
date: 2023/11/21
tags:
    - attack.credential_access
    - attack.t1003-003
references: 
    - https://www.ired.team/offensive-security/credential-access-and-credential-dumping/ntds.dit-enumeration
    - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rioVumJB0Fo&ab_channel=13Cubed
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1003/003/
logsource:
  product: windows
  service: application
detection:
  selection_1:
    - EventID: 325
  selection_2:
    ProcessCommandLine|contains|all:
      - "ntds.dit"
  condition:
    selection_1 and selection_2
falsepositives:
  - "Legitimate administrive backups of the ntds.dit, all instances of this requires investigation regardless."
  level: high